The temptation to attack specific previous postings is strong - postings
that I found unilluminating and pushy.  But instead of posting the
yucky sections from them and insulting the authors, I'm going to put
forth a little more argument for pool confirmation...

Apparently some people think pool confirmation makes the game too wimpy
and others think lack of confirmation makes inappropriate demands on
finger skill/carefulness.
I want to know, if pool confirmation is optional, will the steadfast
no-confirm people be happy, playing with no confirmation for themselves?
If not, are you sure that you know what everyone will find enjoyable
better than they themselves do?  (I'm not accusing you of claiming to
know this...)

And if confirmation is optional but the default is no-confirm, will pro-
confirm people be happy?  I certainly will; I have no problem with a
one-time edit of my .cshrc to set NETHACKOPTIONS.

Hope this has been a productive posting,
